{
  "title": "Lake District",
  "date": "2026-04-06",
  "dateEnd": "2026-04-11",
  "intro": [
    "A few days walking the fells in early spring. Low cloud, wet stone, moss underfoot.",
    "Shot on an old family camera that had been lying around for some time."
  ],
  "outro": [
    "I'd dabbled with the camera over the last few months, but this was the first time it started to click.",
    "No plan going in — just experimenting with light, close-ups, water in motion.",
    "Editing is new for me too. Turns out capturing the photos is the easy part;",
    "it's much harder deciding what to leave out.",
    "Over the last year I've found myself gravitating towards pairing visuals with music,",
    "and this felt like an extension of that — only with a bit more deliberation on the sequencing.",
    "If you scrolled through with The Lark Ascending playing, that was the idea."
  ],
  "location": "Cumbria, England",
  "camera": "Canon EOS 350D · Tamron 28–300mm",
